{"full":"hf:aeesh1/quilltale","spaceId":"aeesh1/quilltale","name":"᚛ Quilltale ᚜","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","storytelling","game","llm","ai-agents","rpg","memory","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":4,"created":"2026-05-22T19:10:50.000Z","updated":"2026-05-26T15:46:55.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://aeesh1-quilltale.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/aeesh1/quilltale","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T14:51:15.171Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T14:51:15.171Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T14:51:15.171Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🪶","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Quilltale is a text adventure powered by an AI Game Master that maintains a persistent, structured model of the game world. The story is generated by a language model. The facts are enforced by code.","Most AI games let the model hallucinate freely. It forgets what happened a few turns ago, invents items that were never there, and contradicts itself without noticing. Quilltale works differently. Every location, item, NPC, and player action is tracked in a formal world model that the AI reads before every response and cannot override. If you leave the dagger on the table, it stays there. If you threaten someone, they remember. If you ask to pick up something that is not in your location, the world rejects it, and the story reflects that reality.","The result is a game that actually holds together over a long session, which turns out to be a significantly harder problem than generating a good story."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/aeesh1/quilltale/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"20b7c50a1f154eeb0ae8d6e2720eef022e8a84f70eb7ec9cb0a7adb0170874ff","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:32:43.883Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T14:51:15.274Z